  "grammar": {
    "title": "The Verb To Be (am, is, are)",
    "explanation": "**Be** is the most important verb in English. It has three forms: **am**, **is**, and **are**.\n\nUse **am** with I. Use **is** with one person or one thing. Use **are** with more than one person or thing.\n\nThe bride **is** happy. The children **are** happy.\n\nFor negatives, add not: **am not**, **is not**, **are not**. Short forms are **isn't** and **aren't**.\n\nFor questions, put **am**, **is**, or **are** first. Short answers use the full form: Yes, I **am**.",
    "examples": [
      "*I **am** a student. (I + am)",
      "*My mother **is** a doctor. (one person + is)",
      "*They **are** from Japan. (they + are)",
      "*It **is** cold today. (it + is)",
      "*We **aren't** ready. (negative)",
      "*Are you OK? Yes, I **am**. (short answer)"
    ],
